        "zoom": [
          1,
          1.06
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Māui frotó el primer palo una y otra vez, hasta cansarse los brazos. La madera solo se puso tibia.",
          "en": "Māui rubbed the first stick again and again, until his arms were tired. The wood only got warm."
        },
        {
          "es": "«Esa no era», dijo el ave. «Prueba con otra.»",
          "en": "\"That one was wrong,\" said the bird. \"Try another.\""
        },
        {
          "es": "Frotó otro palo, y otro más. Y otra vez no salió nada, solo un poco de polvo tibio.",
          "en": "He rubbed another stick, and another. Again nothing came but a little warm dust."
        },
        {
          "es": "Cada vez, ella nombraba un árbol nuevo. Cada vez, la madera seguía fría.",
          "en": "Each time, she named a new tree. Each time, the wood stayed cold."
        },
        {
          "es": "Māui no era tonto. Entendió lo que hacía la madre ʻalae: lo engañaba para proteger su fuego.",
          "en": "Māui was no fool. He saw what she was doing. She was tricking him, to keep her fire safe."
        }
      ],
